  "conclusions": [
    "RuntimeBindings validates the actual Originals class/module file and manifest identities, then imports only the three immutable W2 profile files. It appends owned module names and never replaces an existing module or the original native_core globals.",
    "Each fixed lane creates exactly one W2 CompilerQualifiedProfile. The adapter retains its original contract object and deep-copy witness; validators() returns the same lane adapter, and invocation/enumeration/results all delegate to that original instance. The original profile refuses result qualification before that instance has actual enumeration.",
    "The four original host helpers and eight original Consumer methods are selected unchanged into separate app10 module namespaces. Their native_core global is this finite binding object, so both original host callback signatures receive the same stored lane instance rather than a fresh W2 factory result.",
    "Every entry to an inherited witness-capable profile call first checks the original CommandAdmission. The final unchanged/profile-byte checks are file-only; source/control Git admission remains under commands.is_open. Closed ownership is never cleared by later file observations.",
    "The adapter preserves Bin original target PinkhaAnyUITests while requiring the actual selected compiler target AnytypeTests. Four finite lanes retain3/7,3/6,2/2,2/3=10methods/18cases. G07 exact-method selection and parameterized full-suite rules remain in the unchanged W2 profile.",
    "Activation stays closed by immutable hash, false constants, empty plans and absent final source/native/producer receipts before external path/device admission. Nothing in this source review grants an executable runtime tuple.",
    "The existing first-error/custody handlers are byte-identical; current result constructors do not prepopulate firstFailure with null. No analogous explicit-null regression from the separately reviewed T5 helper is introduced here."
  ],
